Atlas overlay patch 0096: ui/toolbar-glyphs
Why: the toolbar of the reel (scene 3 and 7, pose atlas-ntp-light, still full-52_6) draws the two
buttons the engine paints itself with the WolOS glyphs: open-menu (three lines) for the app menu and
folder-download for the downloads button, with the progress ring around it as before. The glyphs are
the design repository's symbolic icons as vector icons of the toolbar area
(chrome/browser/ui/atlas/toolbar/vector_icons, reached through toolbar_glyphs.h so an engine file
includes no generated header). No setting picks a toolbar icon, so this is one line per button.
Files: chrome/browser/ui/views/toolbar/browser_app_menu_button.cc,
 chrome/browser/ui/views/download/bubble/download_toolbar_ui_controller.cc,
 chrome/browser/ui/browser_actions.cc (the downloads action's first icon)
Test filter: reel-check scenes R02 and R07 (toolbar pair: the menu and downloads glyphs)
Rebase risk: L (one include and one icon line per file)
Release: 0.13
License: GPL-3.0-or-later (hunks in files the inherited series patches)
Verified at: 156.0.8078.79, prepared tree with the inherited and platform series applied

